          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            What are called
            %em advanced
            and
            %em retarded causal Green functions
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Δ
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta_{A/R}
            are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Green+functions"} Green functions
            for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hyperbolic+differential+operators"} hyperbolic differential operators
            on manifolds with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/causal+structure"} causal structure
            (e.g.
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spacetimes"} spacetimes
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/support"} support
            is in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/future+cone"} future cone
            or
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/past+cone"} past cone
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integral+kernels"} integral kernels
            hence say how a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/delta+distribution"} point excitation
            %em propagates
            into the future or past, respectively, via the given
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+equation"} differential equation
            = succeed "." do
              %em propagators
          %p
            If both advanced and retarded Green functions exist for a differential operator as well as for its
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formally+adjoint+differential+operator"} formal adjoint
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Green+hyperbolic+differential+operator"} Green hyperbolic differential operator
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/globally+hyperbolic+spacetimes"} globally hyperbolic spacetimes
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/normally+hyperbolic+differential+operators"} normally hyperbolic differential operators
                such as the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/wave+operator"} wave operator
                and the
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Klein-Gordon+operator"} Klein-Gordon operator
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dirac+operators"} Dirac operators
                on
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spinor+bundles"} spinor bundles
                whose square is a normally hyperbolic differential operator as above.
          %p
            The advanced/retarded
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integral+kernel"} integral kernel
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Δ
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi R
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi 𝒟
                  %mo ′
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ×
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\Delta_{A/R}
                  \\in \mathcal{D}'(X \times X)
          %p is such that
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo ,
                      %mi y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi supp
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi Δ
                        %mi R
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (x,y) \in supp(\Delta_R)
                precisely if
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
                is in the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/causal+future"} causal future
                of
                = succeed ";" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi y
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo ,
                      %mi y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi supp
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi Δ
                        %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (x,y) \in supp(\Delta_A)
                precisely if
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
                is in the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/causal+past"} causal past
                of
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi y
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y
          %p
            Written as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+functions"} generalized functions
            these satisfy
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Δ
                    %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi Δ
                    %mi R
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi y
                  %mo ,
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\Delta_A(x,y) = \Delta_R(y,x)
                  \\,.
          %p This implies in particular that
          %ol
            %li
              the
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/causal+propagator"} causal propagator
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Δ
                    %mi S
                  %mo ≔
                  %msub
                    %mi Δ
                    %mi R
                  %mo −
                  %msub
                    %mi Δ
                    %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\Delta_S \coloneqq \Delta_R - \Delta_A
          %p
            is skew-symmetric in its arguments (reflecting the fact that this is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integral+kernel"} integral kernel
            for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peierls-Poisson+bracket"} Peierls-Poisson bracket
            for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+field"} free
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/scalar+field"} scalar field
            on the given spacetime);
          %ol
            %li
              the
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dirac+propagator"} Dirac propagator
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Δ
                    %mi D
                  %mo ≔
                  %msub
                    %mi Δ
                    %mi R
                  %mo +
                  %msub
                    %mi Δ
                    %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\Delta_D \coloneqq \Delta_R + \Delta_A
          %p
            is symmetric in its arguments, reflecting the fact that this is the integral kernel for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/time-ordered+products"} time-ordered products
            away from the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diagonal"} diagonal
          %h2#definition Definition
          #CompactlySourceCausalSupport.num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              %strong (compactly sourced causal support)
            %p
              Given a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+bundle"} vector bundle
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                    %mi Σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E \overset{}{\to} \Sigma
              over a manifold
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
