          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Klein-Gordon+operator"} Klein-Gordon operator
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Green+hyperbolic+differential+operator"} Green hyperbolic differential operator
              (
              %a{:href => "Green+hyperbolic+partial+differential+equation#GreenHyperbolicKleinGordonOperator"}> this example
              ) therefore its advanced and retarded Green functions exist uniquely (prop.
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#AdvancedAndRetardedGreenFunctionsForGreenHyperbolicOperatorAreUnique"}
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#GreenFunctionsAreContinuous"}
              says that they are
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+linear+functionals"} continuous linear functionals
              with respect to the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+vector+space"} topological vector space
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/structures"} structures
              on
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spaces+of+smooth+sections"} spaces of smooth sections
              (def.
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TVSStructureOnSpacesOfSmoothSections"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Klein-Gordon+operator"} Klein-Gordon operator
              this just means that
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
