          %p
            We now discuss the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/singular+support"} singular support
            and the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/wave+front+sets"} wave front sets
            of the various
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/propagators"} propagators
            for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Klein-Gordon+equation"} Klein-Gordon equation
            on
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Minkowski+spacetime"} Minkowski spacetime
          #SingularSupportOfCausalPropagatorForKleinGordonEquationOnMinkowskiSpacetimeIsTheLightCone.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_11 Proposition
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/singular+support"} singular support
                of the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/causal+propagator"} causal propagator
                of the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Klein-Gordon+equation"} Klein-Gordon equation
                on
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Minkowski+spacetime"} Minkowski spacetime
                is the
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/light+cone"} light cone
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/singular+support"} singular support
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/causal+propagator"} causal propagator
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta_S
              for the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Klein-Gordon+equation"} Klein-Gordon equation
              on
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Minkowski+spacetime"} Minkowski spacetime
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/translation"} translation
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/invariant"} invariance
              as a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+function"} generalized function
              in a single variable
              %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:TranslationInvariantKleinGordonPropagatorsOnMinkowskiSpacetime"} (6)
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/light+cone"} light cone
              of the origin:
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi supp
                      %mi sing
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo =
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mrow
                      %mo {
                      %mi x
                      %mo ∈
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mrow
                          %mi p
                          %mo ,
                          %mn 1
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %msubsup
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                          %mi x
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mi η
                        %mn 2
                      %mo =
                      %mn 0
                      %mo }
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    supp_{sing}(\Delta_S)
                    \\;=\;
                    \\left\{
                    x \in \mathbb{R}^{p,1}
                    \\,\vert\,
                    {\vert x\vert}^2_\eta = 0
                    \\right\}
                    \\,.
          #ProofThatSingularSupportOfCausalPropagatorForKleinGordonEquationOnMinkowskiSpacetimeIsTheLightCone.proof
            %h6#proof_10 Proof
            %p
              By prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CausalPropagatorAsFourierTransformOfDeltaDistributionOnTransformedKGOperator"}
              the causal propagator is equivalently the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Fourier+transform+of+distributions"} Fourier transform of distributions
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/delta+distribution"} delta distribution
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mass+shell"} mass shell
              times the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sign+function"} sign function
              of the
              = succeed ";" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/angular+frequency"} angular frequency
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/convolution+of+distributions"} convolution of distributions
              of the separate Fourier transforms:
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi Δ
                              %mi S
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi x
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo ∝
                            %mover
                              %mrow
                                %mi δ
                                %mrow
                                  %mo (
                                  %msup
                                    %mi η
                                    %mrow
                                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                      %mn 1
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                  %mi k
                                  %mo ,
                                  %mi k
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                  %mo +
                                  %msup
                                    %mrow
                                      %mo (
                                      %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                                        %mfrac
                                          %mrow
                                            %mi m
                                            %mi c
                                          %mi ℏ
                                      %mo )
                                    %mn 2
                                  %mo )
                                %mi sgn
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %msub
                                  %mi k
                                  %mn 0
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mo ^
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ∝
                            %mover
                              %mrow
                                %mi δ
                                %mrow
                                  %mo (
                                  %msup
                                    %mi η
                                    %mrow
                                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                      %mn 1
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                  %mi k
                                  %mo ,
                                  %mi k
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                  %mo +
                                  %msup
                                    %mrow
                                      %mo (
                                      %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                                        %mfrac
                                          %mrow
                                            %mi m
                                            %mi c
                                          %mi ℏ
                                      %mo )
                                    %mn 2
                                  %mo )
                              %mo ^
                            %mo ⋆
                            %mover
                              %mrow
                                %mi sgn
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %msub
                                  %mi k
                                  %mn 0
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mo ^
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\begin{aligned}
                    \\Delta_S(x)
                    \&amp; \propto
                    \\widehat{
                    \\delta\left( \eta^{-1}(k,k) + \left( \tfrac{m c}{\hbar}\right)^2 \right) sgn( k_0 )
                    }
                    \\\
                    \&amp;\propto
                    \\widehat{\delta\left( \eta^{-1}(k,k) + \left( \tfrac{m c}{\hbar}\right)^2 \right)}
                    \\star
                    \\widehat{sgn( k_0 )}
                    \\end{aligned}
            %p
              By (
              %a{:href => "#GelfandShilov66"}> Gel’fand-Shilov 66, III 2.11 (7), p 294
              ), see
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "Cauchy+principal+value#FourierTransformOfDeltaDistributionappliedToMassShell"} this prop.
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/singular+support"} singular support
              of the first convolution factor is the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/light+cone"} light cone
            %p The second factor is
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mrow
                                %mi sgn
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %msub
                                  %mi k
                                  %mn 0
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mo ^
                          %mtd
                            %mo ∝
                            %mrow
                              %mo (
                              %mn 2
                              %mover
                                %mrow
                                  %mi Θ
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                  %msub
                                    %mi k
                                    %mn 0
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                %mo ^
                              %mo −
                              %mover
                                %mn 1
                                %mo ^
                              %mo )
                            %mi δ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mover
                              %mi k
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} →
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ∝
                            %mrow
                              %mo (
                              %mn 2
                              %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                                %mfrac
                                  %mn 1
                                  %mrow
                                    %mi i
                                    %msup
                                      %mi x
                                      %mn 0
                                    %mo +
                                    %msup
                                      %mn 0
                                      %mo +
                              %mo −
                              %mi δ
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %msup
                                %mi x
                                %mn 0
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mo )
                            %mi δ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mover
                              %mi k
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} →
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\begin{aligned}
                    \\widehat{sgn(k_0)}
                    \&amp; \propto
                    \\left(2\widehat{\Theta(k_0)} - \widehat{1}\right) \delta(\vec k)
                    \\\
                    \&amp; \propto
                    \\left(2\tfrac{1}{i x^0 + 0^+}  - \delta(x^0)\right) \delta(\vec k)
                    \\end{aligned}
            %p
              (by
              %a{:href => "Dirac+distribution#FourierTransformOfDeltaDistribution"} this example
              and
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "Cauchy+principal+value#RelationToFourierTransformOfHeavisideDistribution"} this example
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/wave+front+set"} wave front set
              of the second factor is
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi WF
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mover
                        %mrow
                          %mi sgn
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msub
                            %mi k
                            %mn 0
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ^
                      %mo )
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi k
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mrow
                        %mi p
                        %mo +
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    WF\left(\widehat{sgn(k_0)}\right) = \{(0,k) \;\vert\; k \in S(\mathbb{R}^{p+1})\}
            %p
              (by
              %a{:href => "wavefront+set#WaveFrontOfDeltaDistribution"} this example
              and
              = succeed ")." do
                %a{:href => "Cauchy+principal+value#PrincipalValueOfInverseFunctionCharacteristicEquation"} this example
            %p
              With this the statement follows, via a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/partition+of+unity"} partition of unity
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "convolution+product+of+distributions#WaveFrontSetOfCompactlySupportedDistributions"} this prop.
            %p
              For illustration we now make this general argument more explicit in the special case of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spacetime"} spacetime
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimension"} dimension
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                    %mo +
                    %mn 1
                    %mo =
                    %mn 3
                    %mo +
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    p + 1 = 3 + 1
            %p
              by computing an explicit form for the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/causal+propagator"} causal propagator
              in terms of the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/delta+distribution"} delta distribution
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Heaviside+distribution"} Heaviside distribution
              and
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+function"} smooth
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bessel+functions"} Bessel functions
            %p
              We follow (
              %a{:href => "causal+perturbation+theory#Scharf95"}> Scharf 95 (2.3.18)
              ).
            %p
              Consider the formula for the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/causal+propagator"} causal propagator
              in terms of the mode expansion
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:CausalPropagatorModeExpansionForKleinGordonOnMinkowskiSpacetime"} (13)
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integrand"} integrand
              here depends on the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/wave+vector"} wave vector
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi k
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} →
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \vec k
              only via its
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/norm"} norm
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mover
                        %mi k
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} →
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {\vert \vec k\vert}
              and the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/angle"} angle
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi θ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \theta
              it makes with the given
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spacetime"} spacetime
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector"} vector
              via
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi k
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} →
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mover
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} →
                    %mo −
                    %mover
                      %mi y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} →
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo =
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mover
                        %mi k
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} →
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mover
                        %mi x
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} →
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi cos
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
