          %p
            (e.g
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "Feynman+propagator#DeWitt03"} DeWitt 03 (27.85)
          .proof
            %h6#proof_12 Proof
            %p
              By prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#FeynmanPropagatorAsACauchyPrincipalvalue"}
              the Feynman propagator is equivalently the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cauchy+principal+value"} Cauchy principal value
              of the inverse of the Fourier transformed Klein-Gordon operator:
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi F
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ∝
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mover
                      %mfrac
                        %mn 1
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %msub
                            %mi k
                            %mi μ
                          %msup
                            %mi k
                            %mi μ
                          %mo −
                          %msup
                            %mrow
                              %mo (
                              %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                                %mfrac
                                  %mrow
                                    %mi m
                                    %mi c
                                  %mi ℏ
                              %mo )
                            %mn 2
                          %mo +
                          %mi i
                          %msup
                            %mn 0
                            %mo +
                      %mo ^
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\Delta_F
                    \\;\propto\;
                    \\widehat{
                    \\frac{1}{-k_\mu k^\mu - \left(\tfrac{m c}{\hbar}\right)^2 + i 0^+}
                    }
                    \\,.
            %p
              With this the statement follows immediately from the result (
              %a{:href => "#GelfandShilov66"}> Gel’fand-Shilov 66, III 2.8 (8) and (9), p 289
              ), see
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "Cauchy+principal+value#FourierTransformOfPrincipalValueOfPowerOfQuadraticForm"} this prop.
          #WaveFronSetsForKGPropagatorsOnMinkowski.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_14 Proposition
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/wave+front+sets"} wave front sets
                of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/propagators"} propagators
                of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Klein-Gordon+equation"} Klein-Gordon equation
                on
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Minkowski+spacetime"} Minkowski spacetime
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/wave+front+set"} wave front set
              of the various
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/propagators"} propagators
              for the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Klein-Gordon+equation"} Klein-Gordon equation
              on
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Minkowski+spacetime"} Minkowski spacetime
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/translation"} translation
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/invariant"} invariance
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/distributions"} distributions
              in a single variable, are as follows:
            %ul
              %li
                the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/causal+propagator"} causal propagator
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Δ
                        %mi S
